# The skip lines of the allow-list (plan 5.12.4, 5.12.6; M20): with
# --test <path>, a 'skip <oracle>[@<triple>][:<level>] <path> <reason>' line
# whose oracle is the --oracle value (default O3), whose path is the test's,
# relative to the repository root (an absolute path inside the repository is
# made relative), or a directory above it (a path ending in '/'), and whose
# triple and level, where it names them, are --triple's and --level's (plan
# section 12, 'Plan 5.12.6 amended (skip lines)'), makes msil-equiv.py print
# '<oracle> skipped: <reason>' and pass (status 0) without reading either
# image, so the operands here name files that do not exist:
# (1) an O3 line naming this test, under the default oracle and --oracle O3;
# (2) an O4 line naming this test, under --oracle O4;
# (3) an O3 line naming a directory above this test;
# (4) lines that do not cover the test: an O4 line under O3, an O3 line under
#     O4, another test's path, a directory that only starts like this one,
#     and no --test at all; each then goes on to the images and stops at the
#     missing one (status 2), and says nothing about skipping;
# (5) the real msil/utils/equiv-allowed.txt skips O4 of
#     msil/test/M2/00-link/spill-limits.test (spill classes; plan 5.12.6), and
#     not O3;
# (6) qualified lines: 'skip O3@x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil:O2' covers the
#     test with that --triple and --level, and not with another triple,
#     another level, or without --triple and --level; an O4 line with a
#     triple only covers that triple at every level, and an O4 line with a
#     level only covers every triple at that level; an unqualified line
#     covers the test whatever --triple and --level say;
# (7) a skip line whose triple is not an MSIL triple, whose level is not one
#     of O0, O1, O2, O3, Os and Oz, or whose oracle is neither O3 nor O4 is
#     a usage error (status 2);
# (8) the real file skips O3 of msil/test/M1/11-programs/crc32.c on
#     x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil at -O2 only: not at -O0, and not on
#     x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil at -O2 (plan 5.9.9 rule 6; the two sides
#     are equal there).

